EXERCISE 9
Design interactive Power BI dashboards with calculated fields, slicers, and drill-down features
Objective
To design and develop a complete interactive dashboard by combining multiple visuals, adding slicers, and enabling drill-down functionality.
Procedure
Step 1: Prepare the Report Canvas
Open Power BI Desktop.
Ensure data is:
Cleaned in Power Query
Properly related in Model View
Go to Report View.
Set the page size:
View → Page View → Fit to Page
Or Canvas Settings → 16:9
Step 2: Combine Multiple Visuals
Add the following visuals to the same report page:
KPI Cards → Total Sales, Total Profit
Column Chart → Sales by Category
Line Chart → Sales Trend by Year
Table / Matrix → Product-wise Sales and Profit
Arrange visuals neatly:
KPIs at the top
Charts in the center
Tables at the bottom
Step 3: Add Slicers for Interactivity
Click the Slicer visual.
Drag fields such as:
Year
Region
Product Category
Format slicers:
Change to Dropdown (optional)
Enable Single / Multi-select
Align slicers horizontally or vertically.


Step 4: Enable Drill-Down Functionality
Select a visual (Column or Bar chart).
Drag a hierarchical field (Example: Year → Quarter → Month) into the Axis.
Enable Drill-down from the visual header.
Click a data point to drill into detailed levels.
Step 5: Enable Drill-Through 
Create a new report page named Details.
Add detailed visuals (tables, charts).
Add a Drill-through filter (Product / Customer).
Right-click a data point → Drill through → Details.
Step 6: Apply Final Formatting
Add a Dashboard Title using a Text Box.
Apply consistent colors, fonts, and alignment.
Remove unnecessary gridlines and legends.
Add Tooltips for additional context.
Expected Output
Fully interactive dashboard
Combined visuals responding to slicers
Drill-down and drill-through enabled
Professional and readable layout

Result
A complete interactive Power BI dashboard is successfully developed.
